## Day 1 — Linear Regression

### What I Built:
- Linear Regression from scratch using NumPy

### What I Learned:
- How slope is derived from covariance and variance
- How intercept is calculated
- How predictions are made
- Why predictions are not exact
- Concept of error and loss (MSE)

### Results:
- Slope: 0.6
- Intercept: 2.2
- Loss: 0.48

### Key Insight:
Linear regression does not fit every point — it minimizes total error.

### Challenges:
- Understanding why prediction was not equal to actual

### Fix:
- Learned that model balances errors across all data points